---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="byU, Glen Hutajulu"
  description="UX research on how customers report a problem in a digital telco app."
>
<article>
<section class="cs-hero" aria-label="byU complaint journey">
<p class="cs-kick mono"><span class="sq" style="color: var(--acc)"></span>Case study &#123;04&#125; · byU complaint journey · Telco research, 2022–2023</p>
<h1 class="cs-name px-font intro" aria-label="byU complaint journey"><span aria-hidden="true"><span class="c" style="--i: 0">b</span><span class="c" style="--i: 1">y</span><span class="c" style="--i: 2">U</span></span></h1>
<div class="cs-sub">
<p class="lede">UX research on how customers report a problem in a digital telco app.</p>
<a class="pill mono" href="#story">Read the story ↓</a>
</div>
</section>

<div class="cs-cover"><div class="cs-cover-in"><img src="/work/byu/cover.webp" width="2400" height="1280" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" alt="Three phones showing the byU app home, help centre and topic screens"></div></div>
<section class="cs-sum" id="story" aria-label="Project summary">
<dl>
<div class="rv"><dt class="mono">Problem</dt><dd>Customers reporting a weak signal went through too many questions before reaching a solution or an agent.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.08s"><dt class="mono">Role</dt><dd>UX Researcher and Designer (Intern)</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.16s"><dt class="mono">Outcome</dt><dd>Four high-priority recommendations. I do not know whether they were released.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.24s"><dt class="mono">Timeline</dt><dd>Dec 2022 – Feb 2023</dd></div>
</dl>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Overview">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;00&#125;</b>Overview</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<p class="rv">byU is Indonesia's first digital provider and a subsidiary of Telkomsel. It needed a better journey for customers submitting a complaint, and I worked on that as a UX Researcher.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Method">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;01&#125;</b>Method</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">walking the journey first</h2>
<p class="rv">I started with a UX audit, going through the weak signal complaint journey myself to understand what users actually have to do.</p>
<p class="rv">I then ran usability tests and interviews with 5 people who met the byU user criteria. The journey split into three steps: awareness, exploration and complaint. The first two were relatively smooth, so I focused on the complaint step.</p>
<ol class="flow mono rv" aria-label="Journey steps"><li>Awareness</li><li>Exploration</li><li class="hl">Complaint</li></ol>
</div>
</section>
<section class="band" aria-label="Key insights">
<div class="band-head mono"><span><span class="sq" style="color: var(--acc)"></span>&#123;02&#125; Insights</span><span>5 participants</span></div>
<h2 class="px-font rv">what participants told me</h2>
<div class="cards">
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.00s"><b>01</b><p class="who mono">Insight 01</p><p class="big">It takes too many questions to get to an agent.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.08s"><b>02</b><p class="who mono">Insight 02</p><p class="big">Some needed guidance to reach the speed test feature.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.16s"><b>03</b><p class="who mono">Insight 03</p><p class="big">Some did not get the solution they expected. They wanted something quicker and simpler.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.24s"><b>04</b><p class="who mono">Insight 04</p><p class="big">Some felt the data collected earlier was useless once an agent took over.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Quicker solution">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;03&#125;</b>Quicker solution</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">how might we provide a quicker solution?</h2>
<ul class="tags mono rv" aria-label="Recommendation 01, priority high, effort low"><li>Recommendation 01</li><li>Priority high</li><li>Effort low</li></ul>
<h3 class="px-font rv" style="margin-top: 8px">show the default solution first</h3>
<p class="rv">This step is already in the agent SOP and in the Jaringan help articles. Product team data showed 95% of weak signal complaints were solved by these steps, so people should see them from the start. The bot can give the default solution straight away and spare them the rest of the journey.</p>
</div>
</section>
<figure class="fig rv" style="max-width: 1024px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto">
<img src="/work/byu/default-solution.webp" width="2000" height="1339" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="byU chat where the bot replies to a weak signal report with seven troubleshooting steps">
<figcaption class="mono">The default solution appears as the bot's first answer</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Recommendation 02">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;03&#125;</b>Quicker solution</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<ul class="tags mono rv" aria-label="Recommendation 02, priority high, effort low"><li>Recommendation 02</li><li>Priority high</li><li>Effort low</li></ul>
<h3 class="px-font rv" style="margin-top: 8px">reassess the 10 questions</h3>
<p class="rv">Some of the questions matter less, because the answer can come from back-end data or is simply unnecessary. The 10 questions can come down to the 7 that matter most for this step.</p>
</div>
</section>
<figure class="fig rv">
<img src="/work/byu/questions.webp" width="2000" height="1072" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Side by side comparison of the original 10 bot questions and the reduced set of 7">
<figcaption class="mono">From 10 questions to 7</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Recommendation 03">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;03&#125;</b>Quicker solution</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<ul class="tags mono rv" aria-label="Recommendation 03, priority high, effort high"><li>Recommendation 03</li><li>Priority high</li><li>Effort high</li></ul>
<h3 class="px-font rv" style="margin-top: 8px">check the signal directly</h3>
<p class="rv">For comparison, I made the same weak signal report in the MyXL app. Three things worked differently:</p>
<ul class="rv"><li>It refreshes the network connection directly for the number that asked for help, which is quicker.</li><li>A step confirms when the process is complete, so people understand the progress of their complaint.</li><li>People only fill in a form if the earlier steps did not solve the problem.</li></ul>
<p class="rv">In the improved byU flow, the bot checks the APN setting and guides a network refresh, an officer can refresh the connection for the confirmed number, and the questions only come up if the problem is still there.</p>
</div>
</section>
<div class="pair">
<figure class="rv"><img src="/work/byu/bot-refresh.webp" width="2000" height="1339" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Two phones showing the bot checking the APN setting, guiding a network refresh and connecting to an officer"><figcaption class="mono">The bot guides a refresh first</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.1s"><img src="/work/byu/officer-refresh.webp" width="2000" height="1339" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Two phones showing an officer confirming the number and refreshing the connection, followed by the questions if the problem remains"><figcaption class="mono">Questions only if the problem remains</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Speed test">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;04&#125;</b>Speed test</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">how might we provide clear guidance on the speed test?</h2>
<ul class="tags mono rv" aria-label="Recommendation 04, priority high, effort low"><li>Recommendation 04</li><li>Priority high</li><li>Effort low</li></ul>
<h3 class="px-font rv" style="margin-top: 8px">add a shortcut from the chat</h3>
<p class="rv">The speed test was already built into the app, but users did not know about it or where to find it. I added an entry point inside the chat that takes people straight to the speed test page.</p>
</div>
</section>
<figure class="fig rv" style="max-width: 1184px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto">
<img src="/work/byu/speed-test.webp" width="2000" height="1128" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Before and after of the speed test question, with a new link to the speed test inside the chat message">
<figcaption class="mono">The question now links to the speed test. Personal details are hidden.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Status">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;05&#125;</b>Status</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">where it stands</h2>
<p class="rv">This was research and recommendations from my internship. I do not know whether they were released, so I have no results to show.</p>
</div>
</section>
